    board: file CF-161 — the release surface has no contract
    
    The repo publishes no tags at all: `git ls-remote --tags` against the GitHub remote returns
    zero refs and a bare clone of the remote lists no tags, while the local checkout carries two
    `safety-*` markers whose targets (6598ec3, e270fb3) are not ancestors of main. There is no
    VERSION, no CHANGELOG and no version scheme in specs/, so a node that pins a harness range and
    a repo ref has no name for the factory revision it installs. Nothing is tagged: 5 open P0 and
    9 open P1 rows make this tree a non-starter for a first release, and no release contract exists
    to cut one with.
    
    Filed P3 (owner decision on the scheme, then a contract + a selftest arm that fails on a
    local-only tag).
    
    Measurements (all re-runnable) and the rest of the releng pass — gate, board census, public
    posture, CF-156 verified closed live — are in the audit doc beside this row. The pass ran from a
    throwaway clone of the published ref: the registered checkout carried an unstaged tracked edit
    (the sync lane's in-flight `docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md` delta) and 53 untracked judge bundles, so it
    was left untouched. This clone carries no commit hook and none was bypassed; the configured
    checks (`bash tests/selftest.sh`, `bash scripts/boardctl validate`, the gitreins guard battery)
    were run explicitly.
    
